quran[7]{c,v,t}:
  9,87,"And when a (Qur’anic) Chapter is revealed, (saying:) ‘Believe in Allah and struggle along with His Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him),’ the affluent among them ask you for leave and say: ‘Let us remain with those who are sitting back (among the women and children).’"
  9,88,"They are pleased to be among those who stay behind, and their hearts have been sealed. So they do not understand."
  9,89,"But the Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him) and the believers with him strive hard with their possessions and their persons. They are the ones who shall have all the blessings, and it is they who shall be prosperous."
  9,90,Allah has prepared for them Gardens with rivers flowing beneath them; they will remain in them forever. That is the supreme success.
  9,91,"Some of the Bedouins (also) came to make excuses, asking to be granted an exemption for them, while those who lied to Allah and His Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him) stayed back. Soon, a painful punishment shall befall the disbelievers among them."
  9,92,"There is no blame on the weak, nor on the sick, nor on those who do not find anything to spend, so long as they are sincere to Allah and His Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him). There is no reason to blame the virtuous. And Allah is Most-Forgiving, All-Merciful."
  9,93,Nor (is there any blame) on those who came to you (O Prophet) to provide them with riding animals (so that they may join you in the expedition). (But) you said: ‘I cannot find any mount for you.’ So they turned back while their eyes were overflowing with tears of sorrow because they did not find any means to spend.
